## 2. How This Differs from Existing Module B

| Feature | Module B (existing) | Module C (new — Advante) |
|---|---|---|
| **Primary task** | Deforestation / encroachment detection | Parcel subdivision + cadastral record fusion |
| **Input** | Lat/lng centroid, optional GeoTIFF | Scanned cadastral PDF, drone ORI, GNSS points, 7/12 text |
| **AI model** | Siamese CNN (SiameseChangeNet) | SAM segmentation + GNN sub-division + IndicBERT OCR NLU |
| **Output** | NDVI change + alert tier (🔴🟡🟢) | Subdivided parcel polygons + golden record + confidence band |
| **Map view** | `BoundaryMapScreen` (satellite/street/canvas) | `CadastralMapScreen` (parcel overlay + record card) |
| **Backend agent** | `SatelliteAgent` (existing) | `BhumiNakshaAgent` (new) |
| **Evidence injection** | `government_records` at weight 0.30 | `government_records` at weight 0.30 (same slot) |
| **Scoring benefit** | Auto-verified if NDVI ≥ 0.4 | Auto-verified if confidence ≥ 0.85 |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Module C does **NOT** replace Module B. They are complementary. Module B handles temporal change detection (deforestation). Module C handles spatial record resolution (cadastral intelligence). Both feed the same `ScoringAgent`.

